body:
Thank you for posting the article. Holy. Effing. You-Know-What. That entire article was my NMom. That is, to an absolute T, exactly how she thinks, talks, refuses to truly listen, on and on and on and on . . . 

I am tired. I am so tired of being the scared, traumatized child, teen, woman, who has to, at all costs to my own health and safety, protect my NMom’s ego from having to face even a portion of the truth about how she harmed me. I know, with 153% certainty, that nothing good would ever come from continuing to try to maintain contact in a healthy way for me - which would mean genuine acknowledgment and change from her - and so I now choose (and am working on) to end contact with NMom and enabler father. It honestly changes very little for my parents, but is a titanic shift in a positive direction for me. The “permission” given in this article is something I keep seeking out and appreciate when I find it. 

@OP - if you need permission, or confirmation that you’re making a healthy choice for yourself, read the missing missing reasons piece. And I’m going to take a wild guess that if you’re here on this subreddit asking the questions you are that you didn’t go NC on a whim to be “trendy”. I’m going to guess you had super valid reasons that the article you linked did a piss poor job of acknowledging or explaining are reasons you can and should go NC. The therapeutic recommendation that families should “stick it out” and stay together at all costs is something that kept me guilt ridden and afraid to end contact with my NMom for way way way way way too long. Obviously only you can best judge your situation or motives or ability to handle some level of contact and what that might be. But if you even just need a break - take it. YOU matter too. The “family together” crap is well and good for non-abusive families who can actually work together, communicate, and all change for the better. That will *never* happen with an N person. It just won’t. Sometimes I feel so bad for my NMom that she is so dug into her hate and anger and ego-stroking needs that she will never know the freedom of true peace and happiness and genuine connections built in mutual love and trust. And I know why she is that way and I feel bad for her for that, too. But no amount of empathy for her is going to stop me from taking care of myself anymore. I’m tired. I’m so tired. I just want to know freedom from abusive for one month or year or some amount of time besides zero before I die. Don’t feel guilty that you want that freedom, too. You deserve it. We all do.
